# Line endings.
#
# `text=auto` stores every text file LF in the index and converts on checkout, so
# the working tree follows core.autocrlf (CRLF on a Windows clone, LF elsewhere).
# Before this, 488 tracked blobs held CRLF and any tool that rewrote a file whole
# — a python patch script, sed -i — silently flipped it to LF. `git diff` hides
# that (it normalises EOL) while the stored blob changes wholesale, so the next
# commit swallowed the file's entire `git blame` history. Normalising once, in a
# commit listed in .git-blame-ignore-revs, is the fix.
* text=auto

# Must be LF in the working tree on every platform: a POSIX shell or a Linux
# container reads these directly, and a CRLF shebang makes bash report
# "bad interpreter: ...^M" (or "$'\r': command not found" line by line).
*.sh           text eol=lf
Dockerfile*    text eol=lf
*.Dockerfile   text eol=lf
.dockerignore  text eol=lf

# The mirror image: cmd.exe mis-parses a batch file that arrives LF-only.
*.bat          text eol=crlf
*.cmd          text eol=crlf

# Explicitly binary. Git's own heuristic already spares most of these, but under
# a blanket `text=auto` an explicit marker is worth more than a heuristic.
*.png    binary
*.jpg    binary
*.jpeg   binary
*.gif    binary
*.ico    binary
*.pdf    binary
*.zip    binary
*.gz     binary
*.dll    binary
*.exe    binary
*.pfx    binary
*.snk    binary
*.woff   binary
*.woff2  binary
kubectl  binary
